Subject: [PATCH] pin the selected BSS when the driver cannot resolve optional PMF

For normal scan-based association with optional PMF, a driver lacking optional
MFP support cannot select between APs requiring different concrete MFP policies.
Pin the already selected BSS in that case and resolve PMF from its RSN IE.

Keep interface-wide BSS-selection and roaming capabilities intact. Non-optional
PMF connections and drivers supporting optional MFP retain their existing BSS
selection behavior. Explicit ap_scan=2 selection is unchanged. Also resolve PMF
when a BSSID is explicitly pinned: no other AP can be selected for that request.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant.c
@@ -4317,6 +4317,9 @@
 		params.ssid = bss->ssid;
 		params.ssid_len = bss->ssid_len;
 		if (!wpas_driver_bss_selection(wpa_s) || ssid->bssid_set ||
+		    (wpa_s->conf->ap_scan == 1 &&
+		     wpas_get_ssid_pmf(wpa_s, ssid) == MGMT_FRAME_PROTECTION_OPTIONAL &&
+		     !(wpa_s->drv_flags & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS_MFP_OPTIONAL)) ||
 		    wpa_s->key_mgmt == WPA_KEY_MGMT_WPS) {
 			wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "Limit connection to BSSID "
 				   MACSTR " freq=%u MHz based on scan results "
@@ -4499,7 +4502,8 @@
 	if (params.mgmt_frame_protection != NO_MGMT_FRAME_PROTECTION && bss) {
 		const u8 *rsn = wpa_bss_get_ie(bss, WLAN_EID_RSN);
 		struct wpa_ie_data ie;
-		if (!wpas_driver_bss_selection(wpa_s) && rsn &&
+		/* A pinned BSSID lets us resolve PMF even with firmware selection. */
+		if ((!wpas_driver_bss_selection(wpa_s) || params.bssid) && rsn &&
 		    wpa_parse_wpa_ie(rsn, 2 + rsn[1], &ie) == 0 &&
 		    ie.capabilities &
 		    (WPA_CAPABILITY_MFPC | WPA_CAPABILITY_MFPR)) {
